<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="012" project="visual-host-create-button-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>"+" button (CardChrome + VisualHostRoot) + Fluent Dialog host + host-record seed</title>
    <phase>A: Visual Host + Registry + Event</phase>
    <status>completed</status>
    <estimated-hours>4</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>010,011</dependencies>
    <blocks>015</blocks>
    <tags>pcf, fluent-ui, visualhost, frontend</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>PCF UI change across two toolbar paths</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Well-scoped UI addition (a third toolbar icon) with explicit registry + seed contract</model-tier-reason>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add the "+" toolbar icon (AddRegular) between spaarkle and open in CardChrome and the legacy VisualHostRoot toolbar, gated on createWizardEnabled. On click, resolve the wizard via WizardRegistry and open it in a Fluent Dialog seeded with the host record as initialAssociation + lockAssociation=true.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE PCF developer. Fluent v9 + React 18. Follow ADR-021 (dark mode via semantic tokens) + ADR-022.</role>
  <goal>A "+" button appears only when chartDefinition.createWizardEnabled===true, in both CardChrome and VisualHostRoot; clicking resolves + lazy-mounts the wizard in a Fluent Dialog seeded from the host record; unknown key shows a toast.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>design §5.2, §5.5. Host record entity/id/name come from context.mode.contextInfo. lockAssociation hides step 1 (from task 014).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      src/client/pcf/VisualHost/control/components/CardChrome.tsx
      src/client/pcf/VisualHost/control/components/VisualHostRoot.tsx
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      projects/visual-host-create-button-r1/design.md
      docs/guides/PCF-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md
      src/client/pcf/CLAUDE.md
      src/client/pcf/VisualHost/control/components/CardChrome.tsx
      src/client/pcf/VisualHost/control/components/VisualHostRoot.tsx
      docs/standards/MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md
      .claude/patterns/pcf/theme-management.md
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step>In CardChrome iconSlots, add a Fluent Button (AddRegular) between spaarkle and open, rendered only when createWizardEnabled.</step>
    <step>Click handler: resolveWizard(createWizardKey, entitylogicalname); if null → toast "No create wizard registered for {key}"; else open Fluent Dialog with the lazy wizard + WizardHostProps (dataService, authenticatedFetch, bffBaseUrl, navigationService, resolveSpeContainerId, tenantId, initialAssociation={host entity,id,name}, lockAssociation=true).</step>
    <step>Mirror the same treatment in VisualHostRoot's legacy toolbar path.</step>
    <step>Dark-mode: use semantic tokens (ADR-021).</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>Read, Grep, Edit</tools>
  <outputs>Updated CardChrome.tsx + VisualHostRoot.tsx.</outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>"+" renders only when createWizardEnabled; hidden otherwise.</criterion>
    <criterion>Click opens the resolved wizard modally, seeded with the host record; step 1 hidden.</criterion>
    <criterion>Unknown key → toast, no crash.</criterion>
    <criterion>No regression to spaarkle/open buttons; dark mode correct.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    <summary>
      Implemented the "+" Create Wizard button end-to-end: CardChrome icon slot,
      VisualHostRoot's legacy toolbar path, a Fluent v9 Dialog + React.Suspense
      wizard host, and — for the first time in Visual Host — real
      `@spaarke/auth` wiring (previously this PCF had zero auth/BFF plumbing).
    </summary>
    <files-touched>
      <file>src/client/pcf/VisualHost/control/components/CardChrome.tsx — added
        optional `onCreateClick` prop + `AddRegular` icon rendered between the
        AI-sparkle and expand icons, gated by presence (same pattern as
        `hasExpand`/`hasAiSparkle`).</file>
      <file>src/client/pcf/VisualHost/control/components/VisualHostRoot.tsx —
        added: (a) "+" wiring in both the CardChrome-opt-in path (`chromeOnCreate`,
        gated on `chromeOptIn && createWizardEnabled`) and the legacy toolbar path
        (both the inline and float variants, plus widened the toolbar's visibility
        condition so it renders when ONLY createWizardEnabled is set); (b)
        `handleCreateClick` — resolves the wizard via `resolveWizard`, shows a
        Fluent Toast on unknown key, opens a Dialog, and lazily kicks off auth
        init + host-record-name resolution; (c) a module-level singleton promise
        (`ensureCreateWizardAuthInitialized`) so `@spaarke/auth`'s `initAuth` runs
        at most once per page even with multiple Visual Host instances; (d)
        `resolveHostRecordName` — reuses the existing
        `PolymorphicResolverService.resolveRecordDisplayNameFieldName` catalog
        lookup (generic across every entity in `sprk_recordtype_ref`, not a
        hardcoded Matter/Project map); (e) `resolveSpeContainerId` copied verbatim
        from `CreateEventWizard/src/main.tsx:57-67`; (f) the Dialog/Suspense/Toaster
        JSX at the root return.</file>
      <file>src/client/pcf/VisualHost/package.json — added
        `"@spaarke/auth": "file:../../shared/Spaarke.Auth"` (dependencies) and
        `"@azure/msal-browser": "^3.30.0"` (devDependencies, `@spaarke/auth`'s
        peer dep) — mirrors `SemanticSearchControl/package.json`'s exact reference
        format.</file>
      <file>src/client/pcf/VisualHost/tsconfig.json — removed a stale
        `"module": "es2015"` override. `wizardRegistry.ts` (task 011) uses
        `React.lazy(() => import(...))`, which TS rejects under `es2015` (TS1323).
        The override served no purpose visible in this repo (every other PCF, e.g.
        SemanticSearchControl, has no override and already inherits `"es2020"`
        from `pcf-scripts/tsconfig_base.json`) — removing it was the minimal fix.
        Verified safe via a full `npm run build:prod` (recompiles the whole
        `control/**/*` glob, not just the 2 files this task touched).</file>
    </files-touched>
    <host-record-name-resolution>
      Chose to REUSE `PolymorphicResolverService.resolveRecordDisplayNameFieldName`
      (queries `sprk_recordtype_ref.sprk_recorddisplaynamefield`, then retrieves
      that field from the host record) rather than a hardcoded Matter/Project
      field map. This is the same catalog mechanism `applyResolverFields` uses
      internally for `sprk_regardingrecordname` — reuse over new logic per
      CLAUDE.md §11. It is generic across every entity registered in the catalog
      (not just Matter/Project), gracefully falls back to an empty string when
      there is no host record, no catalog mapping, or the lookup throws (mirrors
      the service's own NFR-06 graceful-blank convention), and does not block
      the wizard from opening. Host entity type comes from
      `context.mode.contextInfo.entityTypeName` (confirmed as the correct PCF SDK
      extension property via 3 existing consumers in this repo: SemanticSearchControl,
      ScopeConfigEditor, DocumentRelationshipViewer — none of which are in the
      public ComponentFramework typings, hence the existing `as any` cast
      convention, reused here).
    </host-record-name-resolution>
    <lazy-auth-init>
      `@spaarke/auth`'s `initAuth`/`resolveRuntimeConfig`/`authenticatedFetch` are
      imported ONLY as a type (`import type { AuthenticatedFetchFn }`) at module
      scope; the runtime module is loaded via dynamic `import('@spaarke/auth')`
      inside a module-level singleton function
      (`ensureCreateWizardAuthInitialized`), invoked for the first time only on
      the first "+" click (not on mount). The singleton promise is declared
      OUTSIDE the component (module scope), so every VisualHost instance mounted
      on the same form (they share one JS module registry/iframe) reuses the same
      in-flight/resolved promise — a second "+" click, on the same or a different
      visual, never re-runs `initAuth`. On failure, the promise resets to `null`
      (so the next click retries) and the component falls back to a plain
      unauthenticated `fetch` for `authenticatedFetch` rather than leaving the
      dialog stuck — this degrades more gracefully than the
      `CreateEventWizard/src/main.tsx` reference (which would hard-throw on the
      wizard's first real `authenticatedFetch` call if init failed, since it
      still references the real, uninitialized function).
      IMPORTANT CAVEAT (verified empirically): PCF's webpack config emits a
      SINGLE `bundle.js` — there is no secondary-chunk mechanism for this control,
      so the dynamic `import()` does NOT reduce the shipped byte count the way it
      would in a chunked web app. `@azure/msal-browser` (~787 KiB uncompressed) is
      physically present in `bundle.js` either way. The dynamic import is kept
      because it still defers *executing* `@spaarke/auth`'s module-init code
      until first use (not on every Visual Host mount) and matches this file's
      other lazy-on-first-use pattern (`wizardRegistry`'s `React.lazy()` wizards
      have the same single-bundle characteristic — code-split in principle,
      not in this PCF's actual output).
    </lazy-auth-init>
    <dependency-and-build-changes>
      <step>Built `src/client/shared/Spaarke.Auth`'s `dist/` for the first time in
        this worktree (`npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund` then
        `npm run build` — tsc). It had no `dist/` at all prior to this task (unlike
        the master repo's copy, which was already built for SemanticSearchControl's
        use).</step>
      <step>Ran `npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund` in
        `src/client/pcf/VisualHost/` — resolved `@spaarke/auth` as a symlink to
        `src/client/shared/Spaarke.Auth` (confirmed via `readlink`) and
        `@azure/msal-browser` into `node_modules/@azure/msal-browser`, both
        verified present before writing any import of them.</step>
      <step>`npm run build:prod` succeeds cleanly (webpack 0 errors, 3 pre-existing
        performance-budget WARNINGS only — asset-size / entrypoint-size / "use
        import() to code-split", all expected for a PCF bundling its full
        dependency graph into one file).</step>
    </dependency-and-build-changes>
    <bundle-size>
      Baseline (pre-task, `out/controls/control/bundle.js`): 759,685 bytes
      (~742 KiB) — matches the 741 KiB figure cited in the task brief.
      After this task: 1,250,528 bytes (~1.19 MiB) — a delta of ~490 KiB.
      Almost entirely attributable to `@azure/msal-browser` (~787 KiB per the
      webpack module-size breakdown) entering Visual Host's dependency graph for
      the very first time via `@spaarke/auth`. This is a first-time,
      structural cost of wiring real BFF/auth into this PCF (as scoped by the
      task brief) — NOT reducible by lazy/dynamic import in this PCF's
      single-bundle webpack output (see lazy-auth-init caveat above). Per
      design.md §12 point 9 / spec NFR-01, the <5 KB delta budget applies to the
      FINAL wired-up state across all Phase A tasks, not this task in isolation —
      flagging the number here for the owner/architecture-review checkpoint
      rather than blocking on it.
    </bundle-size>
    <quality-gates>
      <code-review>No Critical issues. Hooks dependency arrays verified correct
        (no missing deps, no stale closures). ADR-021/ADR-022/ADR-012/ADR-028 all
        compliant (see adr-check below for detail). Non-blocking Warning:
        `VisualHostRoot.tsx` grew from 797 to ~1130 lines, past the file-size
        guideline — flagged for a future extraction (e.g. a
        `useCreateWizardDialog` hook) but out of THIS task's scope since both
        files are the POML's explicit `<relevant-files>`. Non-blocking Suggestion:
        `handleCreateClick` bundles several concerns (registry resolution, toast,
        dialog-open, two async bootstraps) — acceptable given they're all
        dispatched from one user action and the two bootstraps are already
        factored into named helper functions.</code-review>
      <adr-check>0 violations. ADR-021: all new UI uses Fluent v9 semantic tokens
        (`tokens.*`) and `@fluentui/react-icons`; no hex/rgb. ADR-022: no React
        18-exclusive APIs introduced (React.Suspense has shipped since 16.6;
        `useState`/`useCallback`/`useMemo` are baseline). ADR-012: new imports
        follow this file's PRE-EXISTING direct-relative-source-import convention
        into `Spaarke.UI.Components/src/` (same as `AiSummaryPopover`/
        `AppInsightsService` already in this file) rather than the npm-published
        package. ADR-028: uses `authenticatedFetch` function reference exclusively;
        no token snapshotting; no direct `PublicClientApplication` instantiation;
        the auth-init-failure fallback uses plain unauthenticated `fetch` (not a
        fabricated bearer token) — a deliberate, defensible degrade, documented
        above.</adr-check>
    </quality-gates>
    <known-gap-out-of-scope>
      `CreateEventWizard.tsx`'s own prop interface (`ICreateEventWizardProps`)
      does not currently accept `initialAssociation`/`lockAssociation` — it does
      not use `AssociateToStep` at all yet (per design.md §5.6, it still bypasses
      the polymorphic resolver with an ad-hoc matter/project map). VisualHostRoot
      correctly passes a full `WizardHostProps`-shaped object (including
      `initialAssociation`/`lockAssociation: true`) through the registry per the
      contract in `wizardRegistry.ts` ("each wizard reads the subset of fields it
      needs"), so today the Event wizard silently ignores those two fields at
      runtime — the host-record seed will not yet visibly lock/pre-fill step 1
      for `CreateEventWizard` until the separate, already-tracked ADR-024
      `eventService` resolver migration task (Phase A, opus-tier per this
      project's CLAUDE.md) lands and wires `AssociateToStep` in. This is a
      pre-existing gap in a file NOT in this task's `<relevant-files>` list, not
      a defect introduced here — flagging for owner visibility.
    </known-gap-out-of-scope>
  </notes>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Plus button gated by config">
      <steps>
        <step>Open a Visual Host visual whose chart-def has createWizardEnabled=Yes</step>
        <step>Verify "+" icon appears between spaarkle and open</step>
        <step>Set createWizardEnabled=No; reload; verify "+" is gone</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Button visibility tracks the config flag; no console errors</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark mode compliance">
      <steps><step>Toggle dark mode</step><step>Verify "+" icon + dialog adapt</step></steps>
      <expected>All colors use semantic tokens (ADR-021)</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>
</task>
